---
import FeatureCard from '@chassis-ui/docs/components/FeatureCard.astro'
---

<section class="home-section py-3xl md:py-6xl">
  <div class="container 2xl section-content">
    <div class="grid mb-3xl md:mb-6xl">
      <header
        class="section-header col-span-full lg:col-span-10 lg:col-start-2 xl:col-span-8 xl:col-start-3 text-center"
      >
        <h2 class="section-title font-3xl md:font-4xl lg:font-5xl mb-xs md:mb-sm lg:mb-md">
          <span class="font-normal d-block">What</span> Chassis Assets Does
        </h2>
        <p class="section-body md:font-lg lg:font-xl m-0">
          Copies the files a designer exports into the output of each platform, with one build
          command. One repository holds several brands and apps, and a brand overrides only the
          files that differ.
        </p>
      </header>
    </div>

    <div class="section-features grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-md md:gap-xl">
      <div>
        <FeatureCard icon="cx-sparkles">
          <Fragment slot="title">Platform Naming</Fragment>
          <Fragment slot="body">
            Renames files to kebab-case for the web and snake_case for iOS and Android. Keeps the
            @2x and @3x variants the designer exported, and sorts them into density folders for
            Android.
          </Fragment>
        </FeatureCard>
      </div>
      <div>
        <FeatureCard icon="cx-rectangle-history">
          <Fragment slot="title">Brand Override System</Fragment>
          <Fragment slot="body">
            Put the files of every brand in the default folder, once. A brand folder holds only the
            files that differ, and a brand file replaces the default file of the same path.
          </Fragment>
        </FeatureCard>
      </div>
      <div>
        <FeatureCard icon="cx-rocket">
          <Fragment slot="title">Multi-Platform Output</Fragment>
          <Fragment slot="body">
            One source tree, one output folder per platform, app and brand. WOFF and WOFF2 fonts go
            to the web, TTF and OTF fonts to iOS and Android. Nothing is converted or resized.
          </Fragment>
        </FeatureCard>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
